.Dd $Mdocdate: November 16 2026 $
.Dt IMAPIDLECTL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm imapidlectl
.Nd show and set imapidle memory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm imapidlectl
.Op Fl s Ar path
.Op Ar name ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
asks the running
.Sy imapidle(1)
for the values it holds in memory.
The default socket is
.Pa ~/var/run/imapidle.sock .
.Fl s
names another socket.
.Pp
With no
.Ar name ,
every node is printed as
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value .
A
.Ar name
prints that node and every node under it.
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
sets a writable node and prints the result.
.Pp
A component that contains a dot is written with the dot doubled,
so a mailbox
.Ql INBOX.Sent
is
.Ql INBOX..Sent .
.Pp
.Ar shutdown=1
asks the daemon to exit the way
.Dv SIGTERM
does.
It does not create a shutdown file, so the next start is not held.
.Ar pause=1
pauses
.Sy mbsync
the way a pause file does.
.Ar pause=0
clears a pause that was set this way.
A pause file is left in place and still pauses.
Every other node is read-only.
.Pp
The reply is one node per line.
An unknown name or a rejected write is an error on standard error,
and
.Nm
exits 1.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/var/run/imapidle.sock
The default socket.
Mode 0600.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std imapidlectl
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Sy imapidle(1) ,
.Sy imapidle.conf(5)
